			<div class="content" id="post-content-4812631">
									

<p>Funny. I read through this, enjoyed tmhe weird legal system affecting SCP, and upvoted, and not once did the idea of pattern screamers pop into my head. When I finished it, I was under the impression that it was something created from the hopes and dreams of all of those lawyers who really want to make the world better, who wish to make laws more just and get things done but are prevented by the very system in which they operate.</p>
<p>I checked the page source but I couldn't find anything hidden in the formatting, so if it's hidden in there it's <em>hidden</em> in there.</p>
<p>Now of course none of this is to say that I think this is a bad pattern screamer skip because I didn't realize it was pattern screamer skip the entire time. I think it's a <em>perfect</em> pattern screamer skip because of that. So, so many mediocre skips are out there are boring unless you &quot;find the big secret&quot; which is usually just white text anyways. This has managed to be interesting all on its own, so much so that me not realizing there was any secrets to be looking for didn't hurt it at all!</p>
<p>+1, would give +10 if I could.</p>

